<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- MYR-434 — privacy manifest for the WIDGET EXTENSION.

	     WHY A SECOND FILE. A privacy manifest is BUNDLE-scoped: Apple reads it from
	     the root of each bundle and the aggregate privacy report is the union across
	     the app and everything embedded in it. `MyRoboTaxiWidgets` is embedded at
	     `MyRoboTaxi.app/PlugIns/MyRoboTaxiWidgets.appex`, a bundle of its own, so the
	     app's `App/Sources/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy` does NOT cover it — before this file
	     the `.appex` had no Resources build phase at all and shipped no manifest.
	     Nothing in `project.yml` needs to change to fix that: XcodeGen classifies
	     `.xcprivacy` as a resource from its position under the target's `sources:`
	     root and synthesises the Resources phase, exactly as it already does for the
	     app target.

	     WHY EVERY ARRAY IS EMPTY, AND WHY THAT IS NOT THE MYR-434 BUG AGAIN. The app's
	     manifest was empty because nobody had checked; this one is empty because the
	     extension genuinely does neither thing, and that was checked:

	       • COLLECTS NOTHING. The extension cannot transmit. `project.yml` links it to
	         `DesignSystem` and `contracts` only and to `MyRoboTaxiKit` NOT AT ALL, so
	         there is no REST client, no telemetry socket and no token provider in this
	         process. Its content arrives push-shaped — `Activity.request` from the app
	         and APNs updates on the `…push-type.liveactivity` topic — and it only
	         renders. Displaying data is not collecting it.

	       • CALLS NO REQUIRED-REASON API. Verified across the extension's ENTIRE
	         compiled surface, which is `Widgets/Sources` plus `App/ActivityShared`
	         (the `RideActivityAttributes` family, compiled into both targets) plus
	         `DesignSystem`: zero `UserDefaults`, zero file-timestamp calls, zero
	         system-boot-time calls, zero disk-space calls, zero active-keyboard calls.
	         There is deliberately no App Group — see the note in `project.yml` — so
	         the extension cannot even reach the app's shared defaults.

	     So the honest declaration is an empty one, and stating it explicitly is worth
	     a file: it turns "this bundle declares nothing" from an ABSENCE that nobody
	     audited into an ASSERTION that `PrivacyManifestTests` re-checks on every run.
	     If this extension ever gains a network client or an App Group, this is the
	     file that has to stop being empty. -->
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
